      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Intracranial tumours causing facial pain are very rare. All previously reported tumours have been located in either the posterior or middle fossa. We present a unique case of a bilateral parasagittal meningioma located in the parietal-occipital cortex presenting with right-sided facial pain."},
